# Keys allowed to sign TAPPaaS release tags (ADR-033 D4). git's allowed_signers
# format: <principal> [options] <key type> <key> [comment]. Who owns each key is
# in SIGNERS.md beside this file.
#
# The rule: a release tag counts only if its signer is listed here AS OF THE
# PREVIOUSLY VERIFIED RELEASE. A key added in a release signs the release after
# it. Retire a key with valid-before="YYYYMMDD" — never delete its line, or the
# releases it signed stop verifying.
#
# Signer keys live in their owner's vault and are valid for one year. The
# recovery key (principal recovery@...) is kept offline, has no expiry, and may
# sign only a release that changes nothing outside .tappaas/ (ADR-033 D4a).
#
# While this file lists no key, the repository signs nothing and every site
# reports it as unsigned (declared). The release that adds the first keys is
# the last unsigned one.
#
# lars@tappaas.org     namespaces="git,tappaas-image",valid-before="20271101" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... lars-2026
# erik@tappaas.org     namespaces="git,tappaas-image",valid-before="20271101" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... erik-2026
# recovery@tappaas.org namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... recovery-offline
